.TH DISCIPLINE.TOML 5 "September 2026" "Discipline v0.12.2" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
discipline.toml \- configuration file for the Discipline CI gatekeeper and diff sentinel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B discipline.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B discipline.toml
is a TOML-formatted configuration file that defines repository policy for
.BR discipline (1).
It controls which static analysis and diff-inspection gates are enabled, their
enforcement severity, file path exemptions, override directive policies, and
benchmark performance regression thresholds.

Discipline uses a strict five-layer configuration hierarchy where every layer
merges deterministically and unknown fields are rejected (fail-closed):
.IP 1. 4
.B Built-in defaults:
Each gate's compiled default is listed under
.BR GATES .
Correctness and integrity gates default to
.BR error ;
heuristic and brownfield-sensitive gates default to
.BR warning ;
gates that need repository-specific setup (a toolchain, a tracker convention,
a packaging manifest) default to off.
.B discipline gates
prints the effective state for the current repository.
.IP 2. 4
.B Repository configuration:
The checked-in
.B discipline.toml
file.
.IP 3. 4
.B Inline TOML overrides:
Supplied via
.B \-\-config\-override
or
.BR DISCIPLINE_CONFIG_OVERRIDE .
Tables merge, lists append, and scalar values replace.
.IP 4. 4
.B Gate switches:
Supplied via
.B \-\-enable
and
.BR \-\-disable .
.IP 5. 4
.B Secret denylists:
Supplied via
.B DISCIPLINE_HOSTNAME_DENYLIST
(appended to the
.B pii
gate; never echoed in reports).

.SH FILE FORMAT
The file consists of TOML tables:
.TP
.B [meta]
Top-level metadata and configuration schema version.
.RS
.TP
.BI version " = 1"
Required integer. Must match the schema version (currently 1).
.TP
.BI name " = \"project-name\""
Required string. Name of the project or repository.
.TP
.BI description " = \"...\""
Optional string. High-level description of the repository.
.TP
.BI mode " = \"enforcing\" | \"advisory\""
Optional string. Default is \fB"enforcing"\fR. When set to \fB"advisory"\fR,
all gates run and generate reports (terminal, SARIF, GitLab Code Quality, JUnit),
but the process exits with code 0 even if violations occur.
.RE

.TP
.B [directives]
Policy for developer override directives (e.g. \fBallow-time-estimates:\fR).
.RS
.TP
.BI sources " = [\"pr-body\", \"commits\"]"
Allowed sources for directives. Valid values: \fB"pr-body"\fR, \fB"commits"\fR.
.TP
.BI allow_hidden " = false"
Whether directives placed inside HTML comments (\fB<!-- -->\fR) are honored.
Default is \fBfalse\fR to prevent stealth overrides.
.TP
.BI fail_on_overrides " = false"
When \fBtrue\fR, any applied directive is treated as a build failure unless
the executing actor is authorized.
.TP
.BI allowed_override_actors " = [\"username\"]"
List of repository actors (GitHub/GitLab logins) authorized to supply overrides
when \fBfail_on_overrides\fR is enabled.
.RE

.TP
.B [gates.<gate-id>]
Individual gate configuration. Every gate accepts these common fields:
.RS
.TP
.BI enabled " = true | false"
Enable or disable the gate.
.TP
.BI severity " = \"error\" | \"warning\" | \"note\""
Severity of violations reported by this gate.
.TP
.BI exempt_paths " = [\"glob\", ...]"
Glob patterns of files exempt from this gate.
.RE

.SH GATES
Every table below also accepts the common fields above. The per-gate keys are
listed in the configuration reference (see
.BR "SEE ALSO" ).
.\" generated:gates
.TP
.B [gates.agents-md]
AGENTS.md exists; CLAUDE.md / GEMINI.md do not fork it (agent-guard; default: on, warning; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.assertion-reduction]
assertion count / strength must not drop in an existing test (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: Rust, Python, JS/TS, PHPT, Java, Go, PHP, C/C++, C#, Ruby, Kotlin, Swift, Scala, Objective\-C)
.TP
.B [gates.vacuous-tests]
new tests must carry a non\-tautological assertion (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: Rust, Python, JS/TS, PHPT, Java, Go, PHP, C/C++, C#, Ruby, Kotlin, Swift, Scala, Objective\-C)
.TP
.B [gates.ignored-tests]
tests must not be newly #[ignore]d or skipped without directive (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: Rust, Python, JS/TS, PHPT, Java, Go, PHP, C/C++, C#, Ruby, Kotlin, Swift, Scala, Objective\-C)
.TP
.B [gates.unsafe-safety-comment]
unsafe blocks / impls carry a // SAFETY: comment (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: Rust)
.TP
.B [gates.deletion-rationale]
deleted files and removed tests need a scoped removes: rationale (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.time-estimates]
no calendar / duration estimates in markdown or the PR body (hygiene; default: on, warning; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.pii]
no home paths, LAN IPs, or denylisted hostnames in tracked text (hygiene; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.agent-scratch]
agent scratch state is never tracked (hygiene; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.shell-secrets]
no command\-line secrets or unverified piped scripts in shell, docker, or CI (hygiene; default: on, error; languages: shell, docker, workflows)
.TP
.B [gates.issue-link]
PR title or description links a tracking issue (#123, Fixes #123) (hygiene; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.commit-provenance]
commits carry the required trailers; an agent\-produced commit carries a review by someone else (hygiene; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.config-integrity]
a change cannot weaken its own discipline.toml without a token (integrity; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.stub-bodies]
added functions are not stubs; existing bodies are not replaced by todo!() / NotImplementedError / return null (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: Rust, Python, JS/TS, Go, Java, C#, PHP, Ruby, C/C++, Kotlin, Swift, Scala, Objective\-C)
.TP
.B [gates.error-swallowing]
no new empty error handler or discarded Result outside tests (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: Rust, Python, JS/TS, Go, Java, C#, PHP, Ruby, C/C++, Kotlin, Swift, Scala, Objective\-C)
.TP
.B [gates.instruction-smuggling]
no invisible Unicode, unreviewed agent\-instruction edits, or instruction\-like text in comments and prose (agent-guard; default: on, error; languages: any (invisible characters, instruction files); Rust, Python, JS/TS, Go, Java, C#, PHP, Ruby, C/C++, Kotlin, Swift, Scala, Objective\-C and prose files (phrases))
.TP
.B [gates.build-hooks]
install and build hooks that gain network or shell access, and package\-manager configuration edits, need a token (integrity; default: on, error; languages: package.json, build.rs, setup.py, .npmrc, .pypirc, pip.conf, .cargo/config.toml, .env*)
.TP
.B [gates.toolchain-config]
compiler, linter, type\-checker, test\-runner and coverage configuration cannot be loosened without a token (integrity; default: on, error; languages: tsconfig, ruff, mypy, pytest, coverage, flake8, Cargo lints, rustflags, nextest, eslintrc, golangci, jest, codecov, phpstan, phpunit)
.TP
.B [gates.scope-confinement]
changes stay inside authorized paths (agent-guard; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.suppression-delta]
newly added linter / compiler suppression annotations (agent-guard; default: on, warning; languages: per pack)
.TP
.B [gates.provenance-tags]
published numerics carry (measured|target|projected) (hygiene; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.ci-integrity]
workflow weakening: continue\-on\-error, || true, unpinned actions (integrity; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.ci-skip-set]
rollup skip set matches each job's `if:` under the observed filter outputs (integrity; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.test-floor]
test\-count ratchet read from the base ref (integrity; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.golden-output]
prevents stealth edits to committed golden/test output files without explicit override (integrity; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.dependency-delta]
manifest diff inspection: zero wildcards, source/license allowlists, and deny.toml verification (integrity; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.test-budget]
property\-test and fuzz effort ratchet (cases, shrink iters, fuzztime, seed corpus) (integrity; default: on, error; languages: Rust, Python, JS/TS, Go, any)
.TP
.B [gates.pr-checklist]
ticked PR checkboxes are reconciled against the diff (hygiene; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.command]
fail\-closed wrapper for any tool: zero\-tests guard, canary, count ratchet (verification; default: on, error; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.sanitizers]
ASan / TSan preset with audited suppressions and a race canary (verification; default: off; languages: Rust, C/C++)
.TP
.B [gates.msrv]
cargo check under the pinned MSRV (quality; default: off; languages: Rust)
.TP
.B [gates.miri]
Miri tiers with zero\-tests guard (verification; default: off; languages: Rust)
.TP
.B [gates.unsafe-budget]
unsafe count ratchet (verification; default: off; languages: Rust)
.TP
.B [gates.bench-regression]
benchmark drift via harness adapters (deterministic counts or BCa intervals) (bench; default: on, warning; languages: Rust, Go, Python, C/C++)
.TP
.B [gates.archive-contents]
distribution archive must contain required paths and zero forbidden developer artifacts (integrity; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.manifest-sync]
reconcile git\-tracked files against packaging manifest declarations (integrity; default: off; languages: any)
.TP
.B [gates.version-lockstep]
version declarations across headers, manifests, and files must remain in lockstep (integrity; default: off; languages: any)
.\" /generated

.SH OVERRIDE DIRECTIVES
When an invariant must be legitimately relaxed, an override directive is
declared on its own line in an allowed source (see
.BR sources ):
.PP
.RS
.B <directive>: <subject> <reason>
.RE
.PP
Each gate names its own directive, for example
.BR allow-assertion-drop: ,
.BR allow-ci-weakening: ,
.BR allow-gate-weakening: ,
.BR allow-dependency: ,
and
.BR removes: .
A directive whose subject or reason is a placeholder is rejected, and every
applied override is listed in the report. The full list is in the gate
reference.
.PP
Example:
.RS
.B removes: tests/legacy_parser.rs parser replaced by the tree\-sitter pack
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All gates passed, or violations occurred while in advisory mode.
.TP
.B 1
One or more gates reported blocking violations.
.TP
.B 2
Could not check: a gate could not run, a required tool or input was missing,
the configuration was invalid, or the base ref could not be resolved. Never a pass.

